{
  "name": "Tackling Interior Home Repair: A Step-by-Step Guide",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Interior home repair can feel daunting, but breaking it down into steps makes it much more manageable. First, you need to properly inspect the damage and identify its root cause. Is that paint peel just old paint, or is there a moisture issue behind it? Fixing the surface without addressing the underlying problem means it’ll just come back. Next, clear the area and prepare the space. This might mean moving furniture, covering surfaces, and ensuring good ventilation. Once prepped, you can move on to repairing the damaged surface or component. This could be anything from drywall repair to patching a hole. Abraham Becerra and his crew at HH Remodeling LLC are experts in this, handling everything from custom framing and drywall to tile and finish carpentry. After the repair itself, it's all about the finish: matching existing textures or colors, painting, and any touch-ups. Finally, don’t forget the cleanup! Make sure the area is spotless. For more complex issues like extensive drywall failure, recurring leaks, or anything pointing to mold, it's wise to consult a professional. They can ensure the repair is not just cosmetic but truly solves the problem.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
